title The guard asleep while its own hazard arrived
prompt the baton; the card's Pheromone line closed on the Rye and shell sweep, and the round open named sixteen files standing on no ref
rota lap 4210, row 0 by count and row 1 by hand -- Air, the row that feels. Lap 4205 read row 0 today, so the rota advanced one by hand and said so. Air's sense is touch, and its fixed seat is Single-Stranded, whose own test is that you check whether a part stands free by trying to pull it out. That is what this lap did to Mantra's weave model: pulled `Line` out of the module and watched two other files fail to move with it. The threshold page names the failure mode in advance -- if the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish -- and a lock reading one of three files is exactly a boundary that exists on the diagram and nowhere under the hand.
think Opened with fleet_round_open, which reported 16 files in the dead-letter box on no ref. The stash_record scan's verdict was ok -- unlanded counts logs, and orphans are reported and gated by nothing. Two whole witness families and a Glow read script stood in that list.
think Cold roster --scoped: 147 guards, 143 green, 2 red, 2 gated, 1217s, tree_moved=no. Held still while it ran (%221), reading the rota row from the closed stacks by named path rather than walking anything.
think Reds first. fold_shelf_link red at fold_depth_lost=5, all five in one peer's shelf. Repaired through the inode so the mode rides, scan back to 0, witness GREEN over 50 readings. Then the rebase showed 5ab5a5dec had landed the identical five corrections fourteen minutes earlier, so mine is withdrawn whole. standing_equipment's red was derivative -- it reads recorded receipts, and the receipt still said red.
think Chose the orphan in my own lane: tools/m/mantra_weave_model_witness.rish with its scan and control, 504 lines authored 20260906 and parked at that round's open. Recovered with git checkout stash@{7}^3 -- <paths>, which reads the TREE, so the 100755 on both fixtures rode across; a git show of the blob would have landed them 100644.
think Ran the recovered scan against today's tree BEFORE touching a line of it, because a guard written a day ago is a claim about a tree that has since moved. It answered disagreements=1 unreadable=1, and the disagreement was the exact hazard its own header had written down in words.
think The cure is not a lap's to take. mantra/src/main.rye writes gen, pos and text into .mantra/ at line 339, so giving its Line a fourth field rewrites a shipped on-disk record, and diff.rye says in its own comments that widening the model is a seam at Keaton's word. So the count is held under a ceiling that only falls rather than a zero nobody may reach.
think Put the ceiling arithmetic in the scan and the number in the one call site, following the cure a peer published today for plant's floor: the scan defaults to zero so every pen and every arriving copy meets the strict reading, and only the witness grants the two known laggards their slack.
obs THE PREDICTION AND THE ARRIVAL ARE IN THE SAME FILE. The witness header, written 20260906, says a hand widening the module would have reddened one lock while two copies stood unmoved. bc37657e8 did exactly that the next day, and the file that said so was in a stash. %499 has been costing parked laps; this is the first time it cost the tree the specific catch a parked lap was written to make.
obs THE LOCK READS ONE FILE. construction/ITINERARY.md names mantra_glow_tend_limb1 as THE LOCK on widening Line. It is a good guard and it reads mantra/src/weave.rye alone, so the widening it exists to gate passed with nothing to say about the two copies. A lock on one of three doors is a boundary on the diagram, which is the air row's own reading.
obs A CEILING AND A ZERO ANSWER DIFFERENT QUESTIONS. Gating disagreements at zero would have made this rung unlandable until a custody seam moved, which is a guard that never sounds. A ceiling of two, proven from both sides on one break, refuses every copy arriving disagreeing while naming the two that stand -- and it falls the lap either is reconciled.
obs THE ORPHAN READING IS REPORTED AND GATED BY NOTHING. stash_record answered verdict=ok with orphans=16, among them two complete witness families. unlanded reads .kyri logs, so a lap of code parked on no ref looks exactly like a clean tree from the guard's side. Named here rather than booked: whether an orphaned source file should gate is a question about how a fleet parks work, and the round-open stash is %499's own subject.
obs Ninth collision inside one hour today. The fold_shelf_link repair was mechanical, obvious, and taken by two hands fourteen minutes apart, which is the claim question the card has asked from four blocks and still has no answer for.
obs THE standing_equipment FAMILY HAS A MECHANISM, not just the word environmental. Its control leg live_leader_parent_reads_gone reds when the roster pass is launched under setsid, because the runner's own process group leader is then parented to init and the control's third reading fires on the real runner rather than on its pen. I launched the final pass that way to keep a timing-out wait from killing it, and paid for it with a red about nothing: run from an ordinary shell, the same tree reads GREEN, control_verdict=ok. Ninth firing of a family the card has called environmental four times; this is the first reading that names what the environment actually was.
obs THE PASS DIED ONCE BEFORE THAT, AND THAT IS WHY setsid WAS REACHED FOR. A hot pass launched with plain nohup ended after 119 guards with a list of greens and no run_verdict line -- exactly the signalled-pass shape REDS %487 describes -- when my own foreground wait command timed out at 590s and its group was cleaned up. So the two observations are one shape from two sides: a long pass is fragile to how the lap that starts it waits, and the two obvious cures each break a different guard.
